## Is a stroke a disability?

Under the **Equality Act 2010**, a condition counts as a disability if it has a **substantial** (more than minor) and **long-term** (12 months or more) effect on your normal daily activities. The law looks at how you would be **without treatment**. Many people with long-term effects after a stroke are covered.

## Returning to work

Take your time. A **phased return**, where you build up hours slowly, often works best. An occupational health assessment can help plan it. Reasonable adjustments could include:

- fewer or flexible hours, and more breaks to manage fatigue
- a quiet place to work, and written instructions
- equipment such as voice recognition software or an adapted keyboard
- changes to duties

**Access to Work** can help pay for equipment, support workers or taxis to work.

## Benefits

PIP is based on how the effects of your stroke affect you on most days. It can affect many activities, such as:

- **moving around** and **planning journeys**
- **preparing food**, **washing** and **dressing**, if one side of your body is weak
- **communicating** and **reading**, if you have aphasia
- **making budgeting decisions**, if memory or thinking is affected

{% checker tool="pip" /%}

If you are over State Pension age, look at [Attendance Allowance](/benefits/attendance-allowance/) instead of PIP. It is for people who need help with personal care or supervision.

## If you cannot work

If your health means you cannot work, or can only work a little, you may be able to get [New Style Employment and Support Allowance](/benefits/esa/) or extra money in [Universal Credit](/benefits/universal-credit-health/). These are separate from PIP, and you can get them at the same time.

## Other help

You may be able to get a [Blue Badge](/support/travel/blue-badge/), a [Disabled Persons Railcard](/support/travel/disabled-persons-railcard/) or [help with home adaptations](/support/home-and-equipment/).

Free, independent advisers, such as **Citizens Advice** or a local welfare rights service, can help you check what you can claim and fill in forms.
